{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Calulate_Positions_Button"},{"__type":"LD","Ix":1,"Var":"HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Transfer_To_Active_Sequence","Y":1},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"In"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"PT","Ix":2,"Type":"TIME","Var":"T#1s"}],"Ix":4,"Name":"TOF","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Q"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"ET","Ix":3,"Type":"TIME","Var":""}],"X":1,"Var":"Calculate_Pos_TOF"}],"LRI":5,"RRI":6,"VLs":[{"Ix":7,"X":1}]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"Calculate_Pos_TOF.Q"},{"__type":"IST","EID":"a4c9acc4-27db-41f4-aec2-a641a2efb918","H":130,"Ix":1,"TXT":"\/\/ Was useful for a shear sequence (Steelway)\u000d\u000a(*\/\/ Modulo between the distance of the Gag Origin and the shear by the Part Lenght\u000d\u000aModulo_Shear_Dist_Gag_OG := ModReal(HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Dist_Origin_to_Shear,HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght);*)\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aFOR H := 0 To 29 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009Seq_Absolute_Input[H].Feed :=\u0009HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Feed[H];\u000d\u000a\u0009Seq_Absolute_Input[H].Punch := HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Punch[H];\u000d\u000aEND_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\/\/Offset the Feeding positions according to the position of the punches in the die.\u000d\u000aFOR I := 0 TO 29 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009FOR J := 0 TO 16 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\/\/ Find the punch offset that corresponds to the the punch for the current feature and add the offset\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009IF (Seq_Absolute_Input[I].Punch = J) THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\u0009Offset_Pos[I].Feed := HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Gag_Pos[J]+Seq_Absolute_Input[I].Feed;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009END_IF;\u000d\u000a\u0009END_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u0009Offset_Pos[I].Punch := Seq_Absolute_Input[I].Punch;\u000d\u000aEND_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\/\/Put the Feed distance back in the part lenght range.\u000d\u000aFOR K := 0 TO 29 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009\/\/ If we have a feed that is longer than the current part\u000d\u000a\u0009IF (Offset_Pos[K].Feed > HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght)THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009In_Range_Pos[K].Feed := Offset_Pos[K].Feed - HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght;\u000d\u000a\u0009ELSIF (Offset_Pos[K].Feed < 0) THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\/\/ If the total feed surpasses the length of the piece then add the length of the cutoff\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009IF (Offset_Pos[K].Feed + HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght > HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght) THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\u0009Cut_Off_Length := HMI_Feed_Absolute_Cutoff\/2;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009ELSE\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\u0009Cut_Off_Length := 0;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009END_IF;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009In_Range_Pos[K].Feed := Offset_Pos[K].Feed + HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght+HMI_Feed_Absolute_Cutoff;\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\u0009ELSIF( 0<= Offset_Pos[K].Feed AND Offset_Pos[K].Feed<=HMI_ABS_Seq_Data.Part_Lenght)THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009In_Range_Pos[K].Feed := Offset_Pos[K].Feed;\u000d\u000a\u0009END_IF;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u000d\u000a\u0009In_Range_Pos[K].Punch := Offset_Pos[K].Punch;\u000d\u000aEND_FOR;","W":400,"X":1}],"CMT":"Offset the position according to gag positions in the die, and put them back in the range of the part lenght","LRI":2,"RRI":3,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"Calculate_Pos_TOF.Q"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Enable"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Feed_Array","Ix":1,"Type":"ARRAY[0..30] OF LREAL","Var":""},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Punch_Array","Ix":2,"Type":"ARRAY[0..30] OF INT","Var":""},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"InSequence","Ix":3,"Type":"ARRAY[0..30] OF Sequence_Absolute","Var":"In_Range_Pos"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Size","Ix":4,"Type":"INT","Var":"Size"}],"Ix":6,"Name":"Sort_Feed","Out":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"OutSequence","Ix":5,"Type":"ARRAY[0..30] OF Sequence_Absolute","Var":"Sorted_Pos"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Done"}],"UD":true,"X":1,"Var":"Sequence_Absolute_Pos_Sorting_Feed"}],"CMT":"Sort the IN range positions so we go from smallest to largest","LRI":7,"RRI":8,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"Calculate_Pos_TOF.Q"},{"__type":"IST","EID":"13001b3e-41ef-46a5-8254-7644a66b2e3d","H":130,"Ix":1,"TXT":"\/\/ Transfer the Absolute position into incremental lenght for the Feed.\u000d\u000aFind_Last_Instance_1(Enable := Reset_Iterator_R.Q, Sequence := Sorted_Pos, Last => Last_1);\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\/\/ Reset the incremental positions each time we sort a new feed\u000d\u000aReset_Iterator_R(Clk:=Sequence_Absolute_Pos_Sorting_Feed.Done);\u000d\u000aIF (Reset_Iterator_R.Q) THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009FOR L := 1 TO 29 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009Incremental_Pos[L].Feed := 0 ;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009Incremental_Pos[L].Punch := 0;\u000d\u000a\u0009END_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u000d\u000a\u0009\/\/ First feed is always itself.\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Pos[0].Feed:= Sorted_Pos[0].Feed+HMI_Feed_Absolute_Cutoff\/2;\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Pos[0].Punch := Sorted_Pos[0].Punch;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009\u000d\u000a\u0009FOR M := 1 TO Last_1 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009Incremental_Pos[M].Feed := Sorted_Pos[M].Feed - Sorted_Pos[M-1].Feed ;\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009Incremental_Pos[M].Punch := Sorted_Pos[M].Punch;\u000d\u000a\u0009END_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u0009\/\/ Add cutoff to last feed\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Pos[Last_1].Feed := Incremental_Pos[Last_1].Feed+HMI_Feed_Absolute_Cutoff\/2;\u000d\u000aEND_IF;\u000d\u000a\/\/ find last element\u000d\u000aFind_Last_Instance(Sequence_Absolute_Pos_Sorting_Feed.Done, Incremental_Pos, Last);\u000d\u000aLast_Gag:=Incremental_Pos[Last].Punch;\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\/\/ Shift the punches since we punch and then feed rather than the opposite, also makes it so the cutoff is always in front\u000d\u000aFOR N:=1 To Last BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Punch_Shift[N].Punch:= Incremental_Pos[N-1].Punch;\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Punch_Shift[N].Feed := Incremental_Pos[N].Feed;\u000d\u000aEND_FOR;\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Punch_Shift[0].Punch := Last_Gag;\u000d\u000a\u0009Incremental_Punch_Shift[0].Feed := Incremental_Pos[0].Feed;","W":400,"X":1}],"LRI":2,"RRI":3,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Dwn":true,"Id":"d8be7943-1ec8-4dc9-9373-2b5e00000004","Var":"Calculate_Pos_TOF.Q"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"In"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"PT","Ix":1,"Type":"TIME","Var":"T#0.5s"}],"Ix":3,"Name":"TOF","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Q"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"ET","Ix":2,"Type":"TIME","Var":""}],"X":1,"Var":"Transfer_Sequence_TOF"},{"__type":"IST","EID":"a28e8b63-328a-4050-a770-2426f8eb7e5a","H":130,"Ix":4,"TXT":"\/\/ Enable the Sequences that will be used\u000d\u000a\/\/ Put the Data into the incremental sequences.\u000d\u000aFOR P := 0 TO 29 BY 1 DO\u000d\u000a\u0009IF (Last >= P)THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009HMI_Feeder_Sequences_Retained.Enabled[P] := TRUE;\u000d\u000a\u0009ELSIF (Last < P)THEN\u000d\u000a\u0009\u0009HMI_Feeder_Sequences_Retained.Enabled[P] := FALSE;\u000d\u000a\u0009END_IF;\u000d\u000a\u0009HMI_Feeder_Sequences_Retained.Distance[P] := LREAL_TO_REAL(Incremental_Punch_Shift[P].Feed);\u000d\u000a\u0009HMI_Feeder_Sequences_Retained.Gag[P] := Incremental_Punch_Shift[P].Punch;\u000d\u000aEND_FOR;","W":400,"X":2}],"CMT":"When pressed, transfo the values into the active sequence","LRI":5,"RRI":6,"VLs":[]}
